[32m+[m[32m## Expression Parser[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe calculator uses a safe recursive-descent parser implemented in[m
[32m+[m[32m`app/services/expression_parser.py`. It accepts the grammar:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mexpression = term (("+" | "-") term)*[m
[32m+[m[32mterm       = unary (("*" | "/") unary)*[m
[32m+[m[32munary      = ("+" | "-") unary | primary[m
[32m+[m[32mprimary    = NUMBER | "(" expression ")"[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA `NUMBER` is a non-negative decimal literal in forms such as `0`, `123`,[m
[32m+[m[32m`3.14`, `.5`, and `5.`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Supported Features[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- The four basic arithmetic operators: `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Standard operator precedence (`*` and `/` bind tighter than `+` and `-`)[m
[32m+[m[32m  with left-associativity.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Parentheses, including nested parentheses.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Unary `+` and `-`, including chained forms like `--5` and `-(1+2)`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Arbitrary whitespace between tokens.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Arithmetic[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll arithmetic uses `decimal.Decimal` so values such as `0.1 + 0.2` are[m
[32m+[m[32mcomputed as exactly `0.3` rather than through floating-point.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Safety[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe parser does not use `eval`, `exec`, `compile`, or any equivalent[m
[32m+[m[32mmechanism. The full grammar is hand-written and only accepts the[m
[32m+[m[32mnon-terminals listed above. Any input that does not match the grammar is[m
[32m+[m[32mrejected as `InvalidExpressionError`. Division by zero raises[m
[32m+[m[32m`DivisionByZeroError`. Both exceptions subclass `CalculatorError`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe parser enforces a maximum input length of `MAX_EXPRESSION_LENGTH = 1024`[m
[32m+[m[32mcharacters, matching the width of the `calculation_history.expression`[m
[32m+[m[32mcolumn. Inputs longer than the limit, deeply nested expressions, and[m
[32m+[m[32mnon-string inputs are all rejected with `InvalidExpressionError` so that no[m
[32m+[m[32minternal Python exception leaks to the API layer.[m
[32m+[m
